        {
          "at": "2026-08-13T21:19:51Z",
          "findings": [
            {
              "category": "capability routing mismatch",
              "file": "README.md",
              "line": 114,
              "message": "The example is not a usable SoTOHE capability entry. `fast-lane` is not defined or invoked anywhere in the template, and the object omits the required `execution_mode` plus the reasoning effort needed at dispatch. Copying it into `agent-profiles.json` therefore fails profile loading instead of selecting DeepSeek. Show a complete existing capability entry or explicitly show only the fields to merge into one.",
              "severity": "P1"
            },
            {
              "category": "capability routing mismatch",
              "file": "README.md",
              "line": 97,
              "message": "The GLM sample connects Codex's Responses transport to an endpoint Z.AI documents as OpenAI Chat Completions only. Current Codex supports only `wire_api = \"responses\"`, so this concrete example cannot connect; the later generic warning does not make it runnable. Supply an actual Responses endpoint or document GLM as Anthropic-only/unsupported for this route. See the [Codex configuration reference](https://developers.openai.com/codex/config-reference) and [Z.AI tool integration documentation](https://docs.z.ai/devpack/tool/others).",
              "severity": "P1"
            },
            {
              "category": "capability routing mismatch",
              "file": "README.md",
              "line": 123,
              "message": "The text implies `model_provider` works for typed-pipeline capabilities, but those runners resolve `CodexCustom` back to plain `codex` and receive only provider/model/effort; the `--config model_provider=...` argument is added only by the generic capability-exec adapter. A configured reviewer or other typed pipeline therefore silently uses the default Codex provider. The accepted “typed-pipeline conformance unverified” caveat covers response compatibility, not routing that never occurs. Narrow this guidance to supported orchestrator-output capabilities until typed-pipeline runners transport the custom binding.",
              "severity": "P1"
            }
          ],
          "hash": "rvw1:sha256:968374b5ea21dafb7da5a0df34d3758b1cac704819c3abe31498a924fea23966",
          "type": "final",
          "verdict": "findings_remain"
        },
        {
          "at": "2026-08-13T21:36:15Z",
          "findings": [
            {
              "category": "capability routing mismatch",
              "file": "README.md",
              "line": 97,
              "message": "README incorrectly classifies DeepSeek as Chat-Completions-only and comments out an otherwise valid Codex custom-provider configuration. DeepSeek’s current official documentation explicitly supports the Responses API at `https://api.deepseek.com` and provides Codex integration for `deepseek-v4-flash` and `deepseek-v4-pro`. Consequently, consumers are told a supported route is unusable and T004 no longer provides the required executable DeepSeek example. Restore the DeepSeek provider block and limit the unsupported warning to GLM. See [DeepSeek’s Responses API documentation](https://api-docs.deepseek.com/guides/responses_api/).",
              "severity": "P1"
            }
          ],
          "hash": "rvw1:sha256:31922a2a84d4892adbb98b3e745e65c071175bce2102fb26905b977c681ef399",
          "type": "final",
