            {
              "category": "action incoherent with the diff",
              "file": "track/items/2026-08-13-multi-provider-capability-routing/infrastructure-types.json",
              "line": 242,
              "message": "`infrastructure::CodexCapabilityAdapter` is declared `modify`, although its frozen-baseline shape and `new(PathBuf, PathBuf, Arc<dyn ProviderSessionCachePort>, Option<TrackId>) -> CodexCapabilityAdapter` signature are unchanged. The intended dispatch-body change is not a TypeEntry shape change, so this declaration cannot detect implementation progress; use `reference` for the baseline-identical type/impl identity.",
              "severity": "P1"
            },
            {
              "category": "per-method error imprecision",
              "file": "track/items/2026-08-13-multi-provider-capability-routing/usecase-types.json",
              "line": 18,
              "message": "`usecase::ModelProviderName::try_new` can structurally produce only `EmptyModelProviderName`, but its return type exposes all eight `CapabilityInputValidationError` variants. The method docs do not name the exact producible variant or justify that breadth, forcing callers to account for seven impossible cases. Use an operation-specific error or explicitly constrain the documented reachable subset.",
              "severity": "P1"
            },
            {
              "category": "per-method error imprecision",
              "file": "track/items/2026-08-13-multi-provider-capability-routing/infrastructure-types.json",
              "line": 18,
              "message": "`infrastructure::ModelProviderNameDto::try_new` merely delegates validation to `ModelProviderName::try_new`, so it likewise can produce only `EmptyModelProviderName` while exposing the eight-variant `CapabilityInputValidationError`. Its docs neither enumerate that sole reachable variant nor justify the broad error surface; narrow the error or document the precise subset.",
              "severity": "P1"
            }
